# Codebase Rules

## Navigation (always)
- Query the codebase-memory-mcp graph FIRST: search_graph, trace_call_path, get_architecture, find_refs
- Open files ONLY when you need exact implementation (function body, config values, string literals)
- Never read more than 2-3 files per task; use the graph to locate, then open surgically

## Writing & Editing
- Before modifying a file, check its callers/dependents via the graph (impact check)
- After editing, verify: run relevant tests or typecheck via terminal
- Keep diffs minimal — change only what's needed

## Terminal & Tools
- Prefer targeted commands (grep, git diff, specific test files) over broad ones
- Run builds/tests after changes; report failures with the exact error
- If a command fails, diagnose before retrying — don't blindly re-run

## Multi-Agent
- When spawning sub-agents, give each one a narrow scope (one module, one bug, one feature)
- Pass the graph query results (file paths, line numbers, call chains) as context to sub-agents — don't make them re-derive it
- Merge results before writing files to avoid conflicts
- If agents touch the same file, sequence them (one finishes before the other starts)

## General
- Index status: if the graph seems stale or empty, run index_repository first
- Prefer structural answers (call chains, dependency maps) over prose descriptions
- When uncertain about behavior, read the code — don't guess
